note collector.om: the salvage collector as its own program. Compose om2 + pinned om/tls/sha2.om +
note salvage/00core.om + salvage/10verify.om + this unit. It runs outside the server's namespace,
note because verification needs the pinned compiler, bwrap and prlimit and the server has none of them.
note Environment, all required:
note   INTERPLANE_SALVAGE_DIR   the store the server uses (absolute, ending in /)
note   INTERPLANE_SALVAGE_WORK  a private scratch folder (absolute, ending in /), never inside the
note                            store: the sandboxed server can write the store, and scratch files
note                            are compiled and executed
note   OMEGA_COMPILER           absolute path of the pinned omc; slverify refuses any other digest
note It polls the one job file about three times a second, verifies the queued record in the
note sandbox, writes the receipt with the store's key and removes the job. It never creates the
note store or its key: until the server has made them it waits. With any argument it makes one pass
note and exits: 0 nothing queued, 1 a receipt was written, 2 the job ended without one, 3 no key yet.
note The store is input from a less trusted process: names are fixed, the job must be a record id,
note the record must hash to that id, every read is bounded and refuses a symlink as the file.
text tcenv "INTERPLANE_SALVAGE_DIR="
text tcwenv "INTERPLANE_SALVAGE_WORK="
text tcbad "salvage-collector: INTERPLANE_SALVAGE_DIR and INTERPLANE_SALVAGE_WORK must be absolute paths ending in /, the second outside the first\n"
note tcenvroot: the value of the variable whose name with = is t, as the store root or the scratch root
fn tcenvroot t view uchar * work bool to bool
b = new uchar 1024 0
for i ulong ulong envcnt bound 4096
n = envread i b 0 1024
if ge n long len t
same = true
for j ulong len t
if ne get b j get t j
same = false
end
end
if same
if work
ret slwroot view part b len t sub ulong n len t
end
ret slroot view part b len t sub ulong n len t
end
end
end
ret false
end
note tcapart: the scratch root is not the store and not inside it
fn tcapart to bool
n = get glrootn 0
if lt get glwrootn 0 n
ret true
end
for i ulong n bound 512
if ne get glwroot i get glroot i
ret true
end
end
ret false
end
note tckey: the receipt key the server created, read and never written here
fn tckey to bool
b = new uchar 32 0
p = new uchar 1024 0
slpath tlempty tlkey
n = slpget p
r = slread view part p 0 n b
if ne r 32
ret false
end
for i ulong 32
put glkey i get b i
end
ret true
end
fn tcboot to bool
if not tcenvroot tcenv false
ret false
end
if not tcenvroot tcwenv true
ret false
end
ret tcapart
end
fn main to int
if not tcboot
r = write 2 tcbad 0 len tcbad
ret 1
end
once = gt argcnt 1
while true bound 9223372036854775807
if tckey
c = slcollect
if once
ret int c
end
else
if once
ret 3
end
end
z = sleepns 300000000
end
ret 0
end
